<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/11th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Cuarte</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1094</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Cuarte was fought in October 1094 outside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valencia">Valencia</a>, months after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/el-cid">El Cid</a> had captured the city. An Almoravid army sent by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yusuf-ibn-tashfin">Yusuf ibn Tashfin</a> to recover Valencia camped on the plain of Cuarte and besieged it, but El Cid sallied out and routed it. It was the first major defeat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almoravid-empire">Almoravids</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberian Peninsula</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-cuarte.jpg" alt="Battle of Cuarte" width="320" height="183" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Icone chateau fort.svg: Lilyu Blason Sainte-Gemmes-le-Robert 53.svg: Manassas File:Batalla de Cuarte (1094).jpg: Esca... · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Batalla_de_Cuarte.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
